    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0255" n="181" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg181"/>

                <head>Sir F. Bruce to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 3, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 1st instant, in reply to the explanation I offered of the
                    meaning of the despatch of Earl Russell to me of the 2<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >d</hi> June, copy of which I communicated to the government of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>It is with much satisfaction that I shall communicate a copy of the note to her
                    Majesty’s government by this day’s mail.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>FREDERICK W. A. BRUCE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
